# Copy this file to .env in the repository root and fill in what you need:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored, so real secrets are safe there. Never put a real token in
# .env.example, because that file is committed.
#
# Who reads what:
#   lod2-api     reads this file at startup (Node's loadEnvFile)
#   lod2-ingest  reads this file at startup (npm run migrate, index, ingest, status)
#   the app      reads the ports below for its dev proxy and VITE_* values (Vite loadEnv)
#   lod2-vision  reads this file at startup (and `npm run vision` passes it on)
#
# Everything is optional except HF_TOKEN, which the vision service needs on its
# first start to download the SAM 3 model. Without the vision service the rest of
# the app still works; only the automatic "Detect openings" button is missing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (PostGIS in Docker, started by `npm run db`)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://lod2:lod2@localhost:55433/lod2

# Port of the database on this computer. Change it only if 55433 is taken, and then
# change the port in DATABASE_URL above to the same number.
# LOD2_DB_PORT=55433

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API (lod2-api)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOD2_API_PORT=8788
# LOD2_API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# fatal | error | warn | info | debug | trace
# LOG_LEVEL=warn
# Browser origins allowed to call the API directly. The app goes through its
# own proxy, so this only matters for other clients.
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Collaboration server (server/, NestJS), started by `npm run dev`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Its projects live in a database of their own, `bauwerk`, in the same Postgres.
# BAUWERK_DATABASE_URL=postgres://lod2:lod2@127.0.0.1:55433/bauwerk
# The app reaches it through its /collab proxy.
# BAUWERK_SERVER_PORT=8789

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vision service (lod2-vision, SAM 3 on an NVIDIA GPU)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hugging Face access token with "Read" permission. Create one at
# https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens after your access request for
# https://huggingface.co/facebook/sam3 has been approved.
# Write it without quotes and without spaces around =, then remove the # in front.
# Alternative: run `hf auth login` once (README step 8) and leave this line as it is.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_your_token_here

# Where the 3.4 GB model is cached. Default: ~/.cache/huggingface
# Point it at a bigger disk if your home partition is small.
# HF_HOME=/path/to/big/disk/huggingface

# Port of the vision service. The viewer proxy follows it.
# LOD2_VISION_PORT=8790

# Python that runs the service. Default: lod2-vision/.venv/bin/python
# LOD2_VISION_PYTHON=/path/to/venv/bin/python
